a reverse-mode autograd engine in c,
built to train karpathy's microGPT as fast as possible.

all memory is allocated statically, TigerBeetle style. nothing is allocated
after startup. ops are recorded on a static stack that each training step
resets in O(1). it uses float64 throughout and builds attention from the 12
primitive ops. matmul loops are ordered for contiguous inner-loop access,
and AdamW uses sqrt instead of pow.


1000 training steps take 0.101s on one Intel Xeon Gold 6426Y core, about
101 microseconds per step for forward, backward and AdamW.


usage:

    $ make parity

    trained 1000 steps in 0.101s
    passed parity check (max abs diff 5.7e-15)
    inference (random sampled name): kaonle


see also:

- discussion on hackernews: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46285424
- counterpart in lean: https://github.com/sueszli/autograd.lean
- original microgpt implementation: https://karpathy.github.io/2026/02/12/microgpt/
